From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohd Ayaan Anwar <mohd.anwar@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:49:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: sgmii-eth: vote for both voltage rails with
 correct current loads

The SerDes PHY has two voltage supply rails, vdda-0p9 and vdda-1p2,
that must both be enabled for calibration to succeed. Without them:

  qcom-dwmac-sgmii-phy 8909000.phy: QSERDES_COM_C_READY_STATUS timed-out
  qcom-ethqos 23040000.ethernet eth0: __stmmac_open: Serdes powerup failed

Use devm_regulator_bulk_get_const() to acquire both supplies and set
the peak current loads (46 mA for vdda-0p9, 15 mA for vdda-1p2) as
required by the hardware.

On the Arduino VENTUNO Q the 0.9 V rail (vreg_l4a) has no Linux vote
from the SerDes. The first SerDes initialization at boot works because
the boot firmware left the rail on; once Linux releases it, every later
initialization (ip link down/up, the TX watchdog reset after a link
change) times out on C_READY_STATUS until a reboot.

Adapted to 6.18: this kernel already enables a single "vdda-0p9"
supply, without a load, in .power_on(); the bulk supplies replace it.
.power_on() does not calibrate here (phy_set_speed() does), so the
error path is the existing one.

Fixes: 601d06277007 ("phy: qcom: add the SGMII SerDes PHY driver")
Signed-off-by: Mohd Ayaan Anwar <mohd.anwar@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Manivannan Sadhasivam <manivannan.sadhasivam@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260804-b4-sgmiieth_serdes_regulator-v2-2-c4bc688177dd@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul <vkoul@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 4f81684a1d1018d7d0e5579f08d95e7701279358)
Upstream-Status: Backport [4f81684a1d10, adapted to 6.18]
Signed-off-by: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-sgmii-eth.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-sgmii-eth.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-sgmii-eth.c
index 5044f2447..b64b8c3a1 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-sgmii-eth.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-sgmii-eth.c
@@ -26,8 +26,15 @@
 #define QSERDES_PCS_SGMIIPHY_READY			BIT(7)
 #define QSERDES_COM_C_PLL_LOCKED			BIT(1)
 
+static const struct regulator_bulk_data qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_vregs[] = {
+	{ .supply = "vdda-0p9", .init_load_uA = 46000 },
+	{ .supply = "vdda-1p2", .init_load_uA = 15000 },
+};
+
+#define QCOM_SGMII_NUM_SUPPLIES		ARRAY_SIZE(qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_vregs)
+
 struct qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_data {
-	struct regulator *vdda_0p9;
+	struct regulator_bulk_data *vregs;
 	struct regmap *regmap;
 	struct clk *refclk;
 	int speed;
@@ -271,7 +278,7 @@ static int qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	int ret;
 	struct qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_data *data = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
 
-	ret = regulator_enable(data->vdda_0p9);
+	ret = regulator_bulk_enable(QCOM_SGMII_NUM_SUPPLIES, data->vregs);
 	if (ret)
 		goto out_ret;
 
@@ -282,7 +289,7 @@ static int qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	return 0;
 
 out_reg_disable:
-	regulator_disable(data->vdda_0p9);
+	regulator_bulk_disable(QCOM_SGMII_NUM_SUPPLIES, data->vregs);
 out_ret:
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -299,7 +306,7 @@ static int qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_power_off(struct phy *phy)
 
 	clk_disable_unprepare(data->refclk);
 
-	regulator_disable(data->vdda_0p9);
+	regulator_bulk_disable(QCOM_SGMII_NUM_SUPPLIES, data->vregs);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -337,6 +344,7 @@ static int qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct phy_provider *provider;
 	void __iomem *base;
 	struct phy *phy;
+	int ret;
 
 	data = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*data), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!data)
@@ -361,9 +369,11 @@ static int qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(data->refclk))
 		return PTR_ERR(data->refclk);
 
-	data->vdda_0p9 = devm_regulator_get(dev, "vdda-0p9");
-	if (IS_ERR(data->vdda_0p9))
-		return PTR_ERR(data->vdda_0p9);
+	ret = devm_regulator_bulk_get_const(dev, QCOM_SGMII_NUM_SUPPLIES,
+					    qcom_dwmac_sgmii_phy_vregs,
+					    &data->vregs);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	provider = devm_of_phy_provider_register(dev, of_phy_simple_xlate);
 	if (IS_ERR(provider))
